WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.560 --> 00:00:05.860
Between the demonic possessions, the psychic
possessions, the star-crossed politics, the

00:00:05.860 --> 00:00:10.360
brainwashing, the drug abuse relapses, and
all of the drama between the team's members,

00:00:10.360 --> 00:00:11.770
Titans can get a little complex.

00:00:12.910 --> 00:00:17.880
Dick Grayson's evolution from Robin to Nightwing
has been simmering ever since the very first

00:00:17.880 --> 00:00:19.400
episode of Titans.

00:00:19.400 --> 00:00:23.189
While he's still dressing as Robin in the
beginning of Titans' first season, the rude

00:00:23.189 --> 00:00:27.800
phrase that shocked fans as soon as the first
series trailer dropped was a signal that the

00:00:27.800 --> 00:00:31.470
Boy Wonder needed to get out from under the
Dark Knight's shadow.

00:00:31.470 --> 00:00:36.790
He eventually burns his Robin costume an act
that earns him no end of ire from Bruce Wayne's

00:00:36.790 --> 00:00:42.380
suit-maker Stu in season 2's penultimate episode
and assures Jason Todd that he's no challenge

00:00:42.380 --> 00:00:44.540
to Jason's role as Robin.

00:00:44.540 --> 00:00:50.210
Eventually he's forced to ask himself exactly
what Todd asks him: if he isn't Robin, who

00:00:50.210 --> 00:00:51.210
is he?

00:00:51.210 --> 00:00:55.010
"New costume, but the same old Dick Grayson."

00:00:55.010 --> 00:00:58.830
Dogged by his own inner Bruce Wayne, Dick
eventually comes to terms with the need to

00:00:58.830 --> 00:01:03.710
evolve beyond Robin, as well as beyond being
merely Dick Grayson.

00:01:03.710 --> 00:01:08.100
When Dick gets himself thrown in prison, he
finds more inspiration from a fellow prisoner

00:01:08.100 --> 00:01:14.090
who carves an image of his home village guardian
Alazul, or "blue wing" in Spanish onto their

00:01:14.090 --> 00:01:16.050
prison cell wall.

00:01:16.050 --> 00:01:21.270
Once he finally realizes Jericho is alive
within his father's body, Dick breaks himself

00:01:21.270 --> 00:01:22.950
out of prison.

00:01:22.950 --> 00:01:27.229
Eventually he makes his way to Stu who, along
with Lily, has already been busy making Dick

00:01:27.229 --> 00:01:28.869
his new outfit.

00:01:28.869 --> 00:01:33.920
In "Nightwing," the titular hero finally arrives
and gives Deathstroke the fight he deserves.

00:01:34.920 --> 00:01:39.420
While we see Slade Wilson accidentally kill
his son in the flashback episode "Jericho,"

00:01:39.420 --> 00:01:42.759
there have been hints for a while that Jericho
was alive.

00:01:42.759 --> 00:01:43.819
"Body hopping…

00:01:43.819 --> 00:01:48.039
There's so much you could do with that."

00:01:48.039 --> 00:01:54.200
In season 2's 11th episode, it's finally confirmed
that before he died, Jericho psychically jumped

00:01:54.200 --> 00:01:58.789
into Deathstroke's body and has been waiting
for the chance to escape.

00:01:58.789 --> 00:02:03.579
As he's reviewing his memories of his last
face-to-face with Slade, Dick notices something

00:02:03.579 --> 00:02:08.810
that escaped him earlier while Slade himself
offered no forgiveness, his hands made the

00:02:08.810 --> 00:02:11.390
ASL sign for "I forgive you."

00:02:11.390 --> 00:02:13.959
But Dick can't save Jericho on his own.

00:02:13.959 --> 00:02:18.640
For Jericho to escape his father's body, he
needs another one to inhabit.

00:02:18.640 --> 00:02:22.599
That's where his sister Rose, a.k.a. Ravager,
comes in.

00:02:22.599 --> 00:02:28.260
At the end of Titans season 2's 11th episode,
we learn that Rose originally agreed to stay

00:02:28.260 --> 00:02:32.989
with the Titans on Slade's orders as his mole,
but in large part because of her love for

00:02:32.989 --> 00:02:36.709
Jason Todd, Rose tells Slade to go to hell.

00:02:36.709 --> 00:02:42.220
Since Jason has left her by "Nightwing," her
loyalties seem iffy at first, but thankfully

00:02:42.220 --> 00:02:47.560
Rose turns on her father and encourages Jericho
to jump into her body to save himself moments

00:02:47.560 --> 00:02:49.420
before Rose kills Slade.

00:02:49.420 --> 00:02:54.300
"Jericho, if you're in there, you know what
to do."

00:02:54.300 --> 00:02:59.439
It remains to be seen exactly how Jericho
and Rose are going to handle being two minds

00:02:59.439 --> 00:03:03.980
in the same body, but considering Rose lets
her brother out to talk to Nightwing right

00:03:03.980 --> 00:03:08.040
after Slade's death, we already know Rose
will be better about sharing than her father

00:03:08.040 --> 00:03:08.540
was.

00:03:09.460 --> 00:03:14.340
On the face of it, Mercy Graves' goals don't
seem very complex she's got dollar signs on

00:03:14.349 --> 00:03:15.349
her mind.

00:03:15.349 --> 00:03:20.110
"Nightwing" opens with Mercy remotely introducing
Conner to a group of world leaders willing

00:03:20.110 --> 00:03:23.320
to pay top dollar for their own super soldier.

00:03:23.320 --> 00:03:27.670
After showing the bidders Conner's super-speed
and immunity to bullets, Mercy tells the group

00:03:27.670 --> 00:03:29.830
to tune in later that night.

00:03:29.830 --> 00:03:34.730
The show Mercy has planned includes triggering
the brainwashed Gar into going on a rampage

00:03:34.730 --> 00:03:38.799
in a crowded carnival, and then sending Conner
in to stop Gar.

00:03:38.799 --> 00:03:40.840
"Help has arrived."

00:03:40.840 --> 00:03:45.180
Once the Titans show up, Mercy keeps the camera
rolling in hopes that seeing Conner beat up

00:03:45.180 --> 00:03:49.450
on bonafide superheroes will drive the bidding
up even further.

00:03:49.450 --> 00:03:54.579
Eventually things don't go as Mercy hoped,
and we learn her unforgiving employer Lex

00:03:54.579 --> 00:03:57.590
Luthor is calling to find out what the problem
is.

00:03:57.590 --> 00:04:02.260
While Mercy wants top dollar for Conner's
super-powered services, it's likely money

00:04:02.260 --> 00:04:04.980
is not Lex Luthor's ultimate goal here.

00:04:04.980 --> 00:04:09.590
In "Conner," the episode that shows us Conner
and Krypto's escape from Cadmus, we learn

00:04:09.590 --> 00:04:13.980
Lex and his people went to great lengths to
successfully create Superboy.

00:04:13.980 --> 00:04:18.620
To do all that just for money isn't Lex's
style, at least not as he appears in most

00:04:18.620 --> 00:04:19.620
media.

00:04:19.620 --> 00:04:24.650
In most likelihood the money is just a fringe
benefit to the main goal getting Lex's own

00:04:24.650 --> 00:04:27.600
super soldiers in place in an influential
government.

00:04:27.600 --> 00:04:28.889
Nightwing brings Superboy back to the light

00:04:28.889 --> 00:04:32.690
Psychic visions and illusions are definitely
a recurring thing on Titans.

00:04:32.690 --> 00:04:37.960
They can be used against the heroes, but they
clearly can also serve as a benefit, sometimes

00:04:37.960 --> 00:04:40.830
even proving to be the thing that saves a
hero's life.

00:04:40.830 --> 00:04:46.090
It's Trigon's psychic infiltrations that bring
most of the Titans under his sway in the season

00:04:46.090 --> 00:04:51.229
1 finale and season 2 premiere, while the
visions Rachel gives Dick are exactly what

00:04:51.229 --> 00:04:53.330
frees him from her father's control.

00:04:53.330 --> 00:04:58.270
The same proves true for Conner in "Nightwing,"
and this time it's both Dick and Rachel who

00:04:58.270 --> 00:05:01.760
enter Superboy's thoughts and free him from
Cadmus' conditioning.

00:05:01.760 --> 00:05:03.940
"Okay, it's all you now."

00:05:03.940 --> 00:05:05.560
"It's us now."

00:05:06.090 --> 00:05:09.760
Why is it Dick, instead of Rachel, who appears
to Conner?

00:05:09.770 --> 00:05:11.820
A couple of reasons seem likely.

00:05:11.820 --> 00:05:16.090
First, Rachel is able to free Dick by entering
his thoughts in part because she and Dick

00:05:16.090 --> 00:05:21.520
have grown close, but no one in the Titans
really knows Conner very well at this point.

00:05:21.520 --> 00:05:26.500
Gar probably knows him best, and by the time
Rachel hits Conner with her powers Gar's still

00:05:26.500 --> 00:05:27.860
down for the count.

00:05:27.860 --> 00:05:32.819
Second, Dick's recent experiences in prison
and his evolution to Nightwing help him relate

00:05:32.819 --> 00:05:38.389
to a teenage boy who's barely had the chance
to figure out who or what he is.

00:05:38.389 --> 00:05:41.430
"Tell me how I can help you."

00:05:41.430 --> 00:05:44.460
Third and finally, it's just cool.

00:05:44.460 --> 00:05:49.639
As the thematic sons of Superman and Batman,
Superboy and Nightwing needed to share some

00:05:49.640 --> 00:05:51.240
screen time in the season finale.

00:05:52.000 --> 00:05:56.460
Initially, once Dick and Rachel's efforts
free Conner from his conditioning, everything

00:05:56.470 --> 00:05:57.500
seems cool.

00:05:57.500 --> 00:06:01.440
Dove hears a young girl complaining that her
doll was left on a ride, so she grabs the

00:06:01.440 --> 00:06:03.510
doll and brings it to the girl.

00:06:03.510 --> 00:06:08.910
As she does, a metal tower damaged during
the melee with Superboy falls toward Dove

00:06:08.910 --> 00:06:10.800
and a group of civilians.

00:06:10.800 --> 00:06:16.229
Donna Troy charges forward and holds the tower
aloft, but the energy from the tower electrocutes

00:06:16.229 --> 00:06:17.229
her.

00:06:17.229 --> 00:06:21.030
She's able to keep the tower up long enough
for Dove and the innocents to escape, and

00:06:21.030 --> 00:06:25.410
finally she drops the tower and collapses,
dead, on top of it.

00:06:25.410 --> 00:06:29.430
It seems strange that something like this
could kill Donna Troy.

00:06:29.430 --> 00:06:34.250
Even accepting that power levels of the characters
in the show can differ quite a bit from their

00:06:34.250 --> 00:06:39.389
counterparts in the comics, moments before,
Donna proves herself to be the only Titan

00:06:39.389 --> 00:06:42.940
capable of holding her own in a fistfight
with Superboy.

00:06:42.940 --> 00:06:47.350
Anyone who can survive a few punches from
a brainwashed Conner should be able to survive

00:06:47.350 --> 00:06:49.430
an electric shock fairly easily.

00:06:49.430 --> 00:06:54.360
But maybe her fight with Superboy is the answer
to how the shock kills her.

00:06:54.360 --> 00:06:59.539
She does prove herself able to withstand hits
from Conner, but not for long.

00:06:59.539 --> 00:07:03.970
It could be that her confrontation with Superboy
weakened her to the point that something that

00:07:03.970 --> 00:07:06.530
would normally only stun her could prove fatal.

00:07:07.530 --> 00:07:12.090
We see the assembled Titans hand Donna's casket
and her golden lasso over to what appears

00:07:12.090 --> 00:07:15.340
to be an honor guard of women on an airstrip.

00:07:15.340 --> 00:07:20.080
These are Themyscirans, the tribe of woman
warriors who hail from the same mysterious

00:07:20.080 --> 00:07:22.780
island as Donna Troy and Wonder Woman.

00:07:22.780 --> 00:07:26.820
It's no surprise the Themyscirans would ask
to bring Donna's body back to their island,

00:07:26.820 --> 00:07:32.430
though it is interesting how their leader
whose name we don't learnlooks at Dick, seeming

00:07:32.430 --> 00:07:35.090
to regard him with a great deal of respect.

00:07:35.090 --> 00:07:39.620
It's likely Donna told her fellow Themyscirans
about the Dark Knight's protege, and it's

00:07:39.620 --> 00:07:43.669
only natural they would respect someone they
saw as an accomplished warrior as well as

00:07:43.669 --> 00:07:45.419
a loyal ally of one of their own.

00:07:46.419 --> 00:07:50.580
In "Nightwing," we see Rachel's powers evolve
in ways we haven't seen before.

00:07:50.580 --> 00:07:55.220
After Kori is shot by Deathstroke, Rachel's
able to heal the wound.

00:07:55.220 --> 00:07:59.750
Later when Gar is still in tiger form and
recovering from the beating he took from Conner,

00:07:59.750 --> 00:08:05.229
her powers again are able to heal rather than
hurt letting her snap Gar out of his brainwashing

00:08:05.229 --> 00:08:08.759
and without the kind of psychic infiltration
she uses on Conner.

00:08:08.759 --> 00:08:13.669
And even though these are the first times
we've seen Rachel's powers manifest as healing

00:08:13.669 --> 00:08:17.620
rather than hurting, it shouldn't be that
much of a surprise that she can do it.

00:08:17.620 --> 00:08:22.110
This is why Rachel leaves for Themyscira with
Donna's corpse she hopes she might be able

00:08:22.110 --> 00:08:25.580
to develop her powers enough to bring Donna
back to life.

00:08:25.580 --> 00:08:29.210
"I should go with Donna.

00:08:29.210 --> 00:08:32.280
If anybody can help her, it's me."

00:08:32.280 --> 00:08:34.669
The island may be the perfect place for Rachel.

00:08:34.669 --> 00:08:39.099
The Themyscirans are more used to the existence
of the kind of magic that courses through

00:08:39.099 --> 00:08:43.529
Rachel, and are probably better-equipped to
survive when her powers go a little nuts as

00:08:43.529 --> 00:08:44.810
they so often tend to do.

00:08:45.810 --> 00:08:50.190
The decision Hank and Dawn appear to make
at the end of "Nightwing" to stay broken up,

00:08:50.190 --> 00:08:54.779
but to still work together in the Titans may
seem strange in light of everything.

00:08:54.779 --> 00:09:00.490
It's sure to bring plenty of tension and conflict
in season 3, particularly if Dawn and Dick

00:09:00.490 --> 00:09:03.810
Grayson's old romance reignites in wake of
the breakup.

00:09:03.810 --> 00:09:07.980
But beyond planting seeds for future drama,
there are some good reasons why the pair would

00:09:07.980 --> 00:09:09.480
make that choice.

00:09:09.480 --> 00:09:11.260
First of all, they've done it before.

00:09:11.260 --> 00:09:16.440
In both of this season's flashback episodes,
"Aqualad" and "Jericho," Dawn and Dick are

00:09:16.440 --> 00:09:20.300
a couple, though Hank still remains on the
team with them both.

00:09:20.300 --> 00:09:24.510
By the end of the second season, the Titans
have become a family once more, and it's a

00:09:24.510 --> 00:09:27.410
family that both Hawk and Dove helped create.

00:09:27.410 --> 00:09:31.670
Whether they're going to continue their romance
or not, they both have good reasons to stay

00:09:31.670 --> 00:09:36.140
together on the team, regardless of the potential
for jealousy or conflict.

00:09:36.140 --> 00:09:40.060
It may not be the healthiest choice in the
world, but considering the kinds of decisions

00:09:40.060 --> 00:09:43.769
both have made in the past, it certainly won't
be their worst.

00:09:45.090 --> 00:09:48.750
Bruce Wayne shows up throughout Titans season
2, but mostly as a phantom.

00:09:48.750 --> 00:09:53.140
He appears regularly to Dick as a part of
his psyche, both to pay tribute to Bruce Waynes

00:09:53.140 --> 00:09:58.279
of old and to harshly force some much-needed
revelations upon Grayson.

00:09:58.279 --> 00:10:02.490
Toward the end of "Nightwing," we're surprised
to learn we got even more of Phantom Bruce

00:10:02.490 --> 00:10:03.870
than we knew.

00:10:03.870 --> 00:10:09.440
In season 2's 11th episode, Rachel, Kori,
Donna, and Dawn all receive different messages

00:10:09.440 --> 00:10:13.910
summoning them to a diner in Nevada where
Bruce Wayne appears and encourages them to

00:10:13.910 --> 00:10:16.600
do what they can to keep the Titans together.

00:10:16.600 --> 00:10:21.070
When Kori mentions this meeting to Wayne in
"Nightwing," he politely tells her she must

00:10:21.070 --> 00:10:25.130
be mistaken because he doesn't remember the
meeting she's talking about.

00:10:25.130 --> 00:10:30.200
Kori offers a possible explanation to Dawn
as to how this could be that the Bruce Wayne

00:10:30.200 --> 00:10:35.640
they met was an illusion unconsciously created
by Rachel, along with all the messages that

00:10:35.640 --> 00:10:37.779
summoned the Titans to the diner.

00:10:37.779 --> 00:10:39.190
There's some proof to support this.

00:10:39.190 --> 00:10:43.519
We've certainly seen Rachel lose control of
her powers before, at one point even bringing

00:10:43.519 --> 00:10:47.420
a killer stone gargoyle to life without her
knowledge.

00:10:47.420 --> 00:10:49.230
So could Kori be right?

00:10:49.230 --> 00:10:50.230
Absolutely.

00:10:50.230 --> 00:10:54.520
But until Titans season 3 at the earliest,
there's no way to know for sure.

00:10:54.920 --> 00:11:00.160
Titans' first season ended with a post-credits
scene introducing Conner and Krypto.

00:11:00.160 --> 00:11:05.050
This time around, instead of a post-credits
scene, we get one right before the credits,

00:11:05.050 --> 00:11:10.080
and rather than introducing us to a new Titans
ally, we see the return of a villain we see

00:11:10.080 --> 00:11:13.920
only briefly earlier in the season Blackfire.

00:11:13.920 --> 00:11:18.829
The alien queen is Kori's sister who led a
violent coup on their homeworld of Tamaran,

00:11:18.829 --> 00:11:22.130
and sees Kori as an unacceptable loose end.

00:11:22.130 --> 00:11:26.889
We see a woman in a grocery store parking
lot buckling her daughters into her car.

00:11:26.889 --> 00:11:31.030
She's about to unload her groceries when some
kind of purplish substance strikes her.

00:11:31.030 --> 00:11:36.709
The woman walks away from the car, transforming
into the much younger-looking Blackfire.

00:11:36.709 --> 00:11:38.051
"What the f---?"

00:11:38.051 --> 00:11:43.060
We first see Blackfire as only a hologram
in "Atonement," but now it looks like she's

00:11:43.060 --> 00:11:45.820
found a way to physically manifest on Earth.

00:11:45.820 --> 00:11:46.820
How?

00:11:46.820 --> 00:11:51.350
Well, the substance that hits the unsuspecting
woman in the ear is the same substance that

00:11:51.350 --> 00:11:55.870
strikes Kori's friend and former lover Faddei
in "Atonement."

00:11:55.870 --> 00:12:00.320
Somehow the substance has the ability to allow
Blackfire to possess the victim's body.

00:12:00.320 --> 00:12:06.710
It could suggest there are already Blackfire-loyal
Tamarans on Earth otherwise, where did the

00:12:06.710 --> 00:12:07.779
substance come from?

00:12:07.779 --> 00:12:10.620
Did it just fly out of space on its own?

00:12:10.620 --> 00:12:15.850
It could be that Blackfire will be the big
bad of season 3, and that rather than demons

00:12:15.850 --> 00:12:21.339
or mercenaries, next year the Titans will
be facing an invasion of body snatchers.

